  "family": "Magnoliaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Magnolia grandiflora 'Little Gem&lt;/em&gt;' is a dwarf cultivar of the Southern magnolia, notable for its compact size and slower growth. The leaves are large, with a glossy deep green upper surface and a bronze-toned underside. The flowers feature fleshy white tepals surrounding stamens on a central receptacle. Following pollination, the tree produces distinctive seed cones, which release seeds encased in a waxy red coat.",
